{
  "dom_id": "step-q136383",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "A particle moves from the origin with a constant velocity of $-3i\\,\\text{cm/s}.$ Find the position vector of the particle after $5$ seconds.",
  "worked_solution": "If a particle moves with constant velocity $u,$  the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\n \nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=-3i.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=5\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(0i+0j)+(-3i)(5) \\\\  & =-15i\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
